==Latin==

===Etymology===
Uncertain, could be a merger of two etymons:
* in the sense "fin", from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)piHn-||backbone, dorsal fin}}, cognate to {{cog|sga|ind||end, point}}, {{cog|xto|spin||hook}}, {{cog|sa|tr=sphyá|स्फ्य||splinter, staff}}, {{cog|en|fin}};
* in other senses, a dialectal form of {{m|la|penna}} with either pre-nasal (as in {{m|la|dignus}}) or post-labial (as in {{m|la|firmus}}) raising, from {{der|la|itc-pro|*petnā}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*péth₂r̥|*péth₂r̥ ~ pth₂én-|feather, wing}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*peth₂-||to fly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pinna}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|pinna<1>}}

# {{alternative form of|la|penna|t=wing, feather}}
# a [[fin]]
# a [[merlon]], [[cop]] {{gl|the raised part of a [[parapet]] or [[battlement]]}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} a [[peg]], [[pin]], [[bolt]]
#: {{uxi|la|ad pinnās bibere|to drink in large quantities or competitively|q1=idiom|q2=perh. referring to pins set inside drinking cups to mark exact quantities}}

====Usage notes====
* Senses (2), (3) and (4) are not found for the form {{l|la|penna}}.

